# `.hermes/` is instance-local runtime/session state for a deployed Creator
# Engine instance (live `STATE.md`, handoffs, tmux/pane facts, etc.). Upstream
# protocols and templates live under `docs/operations/` and `templates/`.
# Do not unignore `.hermes/`; do not commit live instance state upstream.
.hermes/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Claude Code local settings override (CC-G-C / D4). A gitignored local-override
# source must never be committed: it could silently weaken or disable the
# committed Ring 1 hook-pack. Governed launches also pin `--setting-sources
# project` to exclude `local`. See docs/operations/CLAUDE_CODE_HOOK_PACK.md.
.claude/settings.local.json

# G2.003.1 CE-event runtime instance state. `.ce/ce-events/spool/` is the
# local, generated append-only CE-event chain zone the `ce event` runtime writes
# (head manifests + per-block files). It is instance-local runtime state, never
# tracked. This is a minimal, additive instance-zone line: do NOT wholesale-
# ignore `.ce/` — governance subtrees under `.ce/` must remain trackable.
.ce/ce-events/spool/

# G2.004.1 PCL runtime cache. `.ce/pcl/records/` is the per-repo authoritative,
# tracked-or-synced coordination ledger (NOT ignored) the `ce pcl` runtime writes;
# `.ce/pcl/cache/` holds only rebuildable index/merge projections and is
# instance-local, never tracked. Additive instance-zone line only.
.ce/pcl/cache/

# G2.005.1 connector read-only runtime cache. `.ce/connector/cache/` holds only
# rebuildable read-receipts the `ce connector` runtime writes; it is instance-local,
# never tracked, and never carries a credential value. Additive instance-zone line.
.ce/connector/cache/

# Instance-local governed-execution working zones. CE gate execution provisions
# per-gate git worktrees and per-PR reviewer-seat clones INSIDE the repo dir
# (`ce-worktrees/<gate>/`, `ce-review-venues/pr<N>-<ts>/`). These are separate
# working trees / clones — never content of the canonical tree — so they MUST NOT
# be tracked or appear as untracked pollution on other branches. Additive
# instance-zone lines only.
/ce-worktrees/
/ce-review-venues/
